{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "nr-construction-state",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.5 step 7e: the `nr-construction-state` RunSpec computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE -- the whole of Michigan, August 2020, weekday, the Construction sector, gasoline, THC, CO, NOx, SO2 and PM10. The first STATE-level run: 100 equipment points over 25 SCCs, 471 cohorts, 2,355 rows.\n\nA STATE RUN IS A COUNTY RUN AT A COUNTY MOVES BUILDS. `PreAggSTATE.sql` makes Michigan a pseudo-county 26000 with a pseudo-zone 260000 whose `ZoneMonthHour` is `Sum(temperature x actFract)` over the state's 83 zones, and a fuel region 26 that no national `nrFuelSupply` row belongs to -- so `DefaultDataMaker` gives it gasoline formulation 12, which the default database does not have, and the `.OPT` packet's queries then fall back to formulation 10 for the sulfur (func A) and find no oxygen at all. None of that is in a table this document can read; all of it is in the model now (`zone_runWeight`, `rsu_*`, `run_defaultGasolineSulfurWeightPercent`), and at a real county each piece reduces to the formula it replaced, so the county runs kept their bytes.\n\nIT FOUND THREE THINGS, in order. SO2 was 0 until the formulation-10 fallback. Every 4-stroke gasoline THC, CO and NOx cell was then off by the exact ratio its temperature coefficient gives for +0.0049 degF: the state's zone weights sum to 0.9999322, not 1, because each county's share is rounded to six decimals first, and MOVES does not renormalize -- so the temperature is `Sum(w x T) / 13`, not a weighted mean. And 35 cells in six SCCs were off by up to 9.2e-4, whole cohorts at a time: model years whose `agedist.f` residual is a cancellation, where the growth indicator's interpolation had been associated `(dv x dy) / dx` where `grwfac.f` computes `(dv / dx) x dy`. One ulp, amplified a thousandfold. All 2,355 rows then reproduce at 6.615e-06."
  },
  "domain": {
    "element_type": "Float32"
  },
